  "summary": "Recent preprints extend exactly solvable Kitaev-type and lattice models to non-Hermitian, hyperbolic, and fragmented settings.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is exact or analytically controlled treatment of quantum lattice models. Preprints in this set apply algebraic, field-theoretic, and geometric tools to models with nontrivial spectral or entanglement structure. One work gives a SUSY/paraSUSY lifting construction that generates Hilbert-space fragmentation from arbitrary finite-dimensional lattice Hamiltonians. A non-Hermitian Kitaev chain with unequal pairing amplitudes exhibits an exceptional point where many-body energies collapse, accompanied by Lifshitz criticality. The three-colored Kitaev model is analyzed on finite hyperbolic periodic-boundary clusters, examining ground-state flux sectors and two-vison gaps. Separately, an entropic order parameter for charge transfer between two intervals is computed via replica twisted partition functions, with exact results for free fermions. What is new is the combination of exact solvability with diagnostics of fragmentation, exceptional spectra, and entanglement-based charge transfer.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
